+// The matmul op uses these kernels for the verify step of speculative decoding, where the DDR
+// stream of the weights is the cost and more activation rows are almost free. Without them the op
+// calls the 32x2 kernel per row pair and the 32x1 kernel for the last row, thus 3 rows read and
+// unpack each weight tile twice, and 4 rows twice.
